N1  - Carson Valley News (Genoa, NV), June 23, 1876, p. 3; May 29, 1877, p. 3; June 15, 1877, p. 3; June 22, 1877, p. 3; March 22, 1878, p. 3. The Morrisites of Carson Valley and William W. Davies. June 1876: “old man Robert Roberts,” who claims to be the Prophet Daniel, visits Genoa and says that the child “who is to ‘run’ the Kingdom of God on earth” is already born at Walla Walla; a small Morrisite meeting in the court house hears R. J. Livingston, then Roberts. May 1877: Livingston, “a long-time resident and rancher of Douglas County,” leaves on May 28 for “the Holy Land—Walla Walla.” June 1877: Livingston’s party passes Reno (from the Reno Gazette), and “Robert Roberts, the Morrisite Mormon who claims to be the Prophet Daniel,” is in town again. March 1878: Livingston’s letter from Mill Creek, Walla Walla, March 2, on the 440-acre farm he has bought. Roberts was Davies’s missionary (see People). The 1877 story was reprinted in the Salt Lake Herald, June 16, 1877, and other papers. Listed on https://morrisite.org/newspapers.html#np-1877
