N1  - The Sun (New York), November 14, 1878, p. 1. “Mr. Wood of Walla-Walla. A Curious Person Who Wishes to See the Rev. Dr. Tyng.” Davies’s missionary S. W. Wood, on his way to England with a proclamation “that the Messiah had come,” tells the Sun that Davies learned in Montana in 1866 that he was the Standard of Israel and then the Comforter; that the society near Walla Walla is called by some the “Redemptionists,” has a tabernacle, a meeting house and a press, and has “no marrying”; and that the Messiah, “the Father’s Son,” was born in 1868 and is ten years old. The Rev. Stephen H. Tyng Jr. says he has had documents from the organization. Checked against the page image. Summarized in the Puget Sound Argus, December 12, 1878 (next entry). Listed on https://morrisite.org/newspapers.html#np-1877
