N1  - Salt Lake Herald (semi-weekly), Friday, March 11, 1904. “On Trial for His Reason.” Also Salt Lake Telegram, March 9, 1904, “Alleged to Be Insane.” William Jones of Blaine, Davis County, in his eightieth year, called the man “who caused the Morrisite War,” faces his daughters’ petition for a guardian (Second District Court, probate division, sitting at Ogden); the report recalls that he was held prisoner by the Morrisites, escaped and came back with the militia, and was a witness for the defense at Burton’s trial. The Telegram (p. 10) and the daily Herald (p. 1) carry the same report on March 9, 1904; the Telegram and gives his age as 80, which fits William J. Jones of the roll, born in 1825. The Herald clipping shows only “Friday, Mar[ch]” and the dateline “Ogden, March 8”; its date is the next Friday. Herald clipping at South Weber City. Other links: daily <i>Herald</i>, March 9, p. 1: https://newspapers.lib.utah.edu/details?id=12207568 Listed on https://morrisite.org/newspapers.html#np-1901
