N1  - Herald Journal (Logan), May 15, 1988, p. 47. “John Bear: Mission to Providence.” John Lebrecht Bear, a Swiss convert at Providence, Cache Valley, left for Kington Fort about August 15, 1861, with at least four other Providence families; his wife and child were killed by the posse’s cannon in June 1862. He went to Soda Springs, married a fellow Morrisite there in 1863, and later joined the Reorganized Church. Drawn in part from his unpublished autobiography. Listed on https://morrisite.org/newspapers.html#np-1951
